   $q$The draft never states the writer's claim directly. Which sentence, added after sentence (2), would best state the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many students and teachers have noticed birds flying near the new science wing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-claim"},{"text":"To protect birds and give students a real science project, Hollis High should apply bird-safe film to the science wing's windows.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Hollis High should close the science wing until the bird problem is completely solved.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"claim-not-supported"},{"text":"Birds face many dangers in the modern world, and windows are only one of them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To protect birds and give students a real science project, Hollis High should apply bird-safe film to the science wing's windows.$q$, $q$The rest of the draft argues for window film, so the claim must name that solution and the reasons for it. Closing the wing is a position the draft never supports, and the sentence about noticing birds is a fact, not a claim.$q$, 'draft', '01da2e99-0526-5bce-96ed-454544918009')
