   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (13) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The council should also repave the paths and add new lights in the park.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Because restoration costs less than replacement, saves a rare landmark and would bring residents back to the park, the council should repair the bandstand.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In the end, music is an important part of every community's life.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Repairs cost $38,000, which is a lot of money for any small town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-opposing-point"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because restoration costs less than replacement, saves a rare landmark and would bring residents back to the park, the council should repair the bandstand.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion gathers the cost, history and community reasons from all three paragraphs and restates the claim. The sentence about the $38,000 cost repeats the opponents' point without answering it.$q$, 'draft', 'b643b1e3-f9c4-5906-84b2-ce90f12f9dca')
