  ('54e6940f-b20d-55bb-90b3-0b04018a0edf', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The draft ends without a conclusion. Which sentence would best conclude the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The wall would cost about $15,000, which the school would have to find somewhere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-detail-only"},{"text":"Once the wall is built, every single student at Brenford will love gym class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"After the climbing wall is built, Brenford should also consider adding a swimming pool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"A climbing wall would get more students moving, it would be carefully supervised, and it could be paid for without new school funds.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A climbing wall would get more students moving, it would be carefully supervised, and it could be paid for without new school funds.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion sums up the three parts of the argument: participation, safety and funding. The claim that every student will love gym goes beyond the evidence, since Ridley Falls reached 70 percent, not 100.$q$, 'draft', 'f54c81d7-40db-5110-8d07-8ec5413721fd')
