  ('47266092-c349-5a2f-8532-ab682a516678', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence (11), would best support the claim that the program benefits the volunteers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Conference nights at Larchmont usually last from five until eight in the evening.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Many hospitals and businesses hire people who can speak more than one language.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-without-evidence"},{"text":"Some parents would rather bring their own family members to interpret for them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-opposing-view"},{"text":"In a survey of Westbury's volunteers, 85 percent said interpreting made them more confident speaking to adults.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In a survey of Westbury's volunteers, 85 percent said interpreting made them more confident speaking to adults.$q$, $q$The survey gives evidence about what volunteers actually gained, which supports sentence (10). The sentence about hospitals and businesses only restates the career point in sentence (11) without showing any benefit to student volunteers.$q$, 'draft', '53bae41c-9b40-5fc1-9fa4-1bdcdbb430d1')
