-- Passage wg9-argument-writing-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('c02e7959-c79e-51f0-b3d8-c97d30e469cc', 'wg9-argument-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Orchard at Ventry Farm Museum$q$, $q$(1) The Ventry Farm Museum shows visitors how families in the valley farmed a century ago. (2) Behind its barn stands an orchard of forty apple trees planted in the 1890s, including six varieties that are no longer sold by any nursery. (3) The museum board has proposed clearing the orchard to build a larger parking lot. (4) The board should keep the orchard and care for it as a living part of the museum's collection. (5) Old apple varieties carry traits that modern growers value, such as resistance to certain diseases and the ability to survive late frosts. (6) Researchers at Hadley Agricultural College have already asked to take cuttings from three of the Ventry trees for their seed bank. (7) Apples come in many colors, including red, yellow and green.

(8) The board says the current lot fills up on festival weekends, and visitors sometimes park along the narrow road. (9) That problem is real, but it happens on only about six weekends a year. (10) On those days, the museum could use the empty field across the road, which a neighbor has offered for overflow parking.

(11) The orchard could also become one of the museum's main attractions. (12) Each fall, school groups could pick apples, press cider and compare the old varieties to the ones sold in stores today. (13) Clearly, the board must protect the orchard, because history matters.$q$, 'draft')
