insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('80e67d3f-ef82-5c99-9fcf-c7cd1d62c4e4', 'wg9-argument-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Student Radio Station at Quinlan High$q$, $q$(1) Every morning, Quinlan High School's announcements are read over a crackling speaker by whichever office worker has time. (2) Most students tune them out. (3) Quinlan should launch a student-run internet radio station that delivers the morning announcements and broadcasts student programs during lunch. (4) A station would give students real practice in writing, speaking and audio editing. (5) At Ferris Valley High, students in the radio club wrote and produced more than 300 short segments last year, from sports recaps to interviews with local artists. (6) Students would also learn teamwork, since every broadcast requires writers, hosts and technicians to work together on a tight schedule.

(7) Some teachers worry that the station would distract students from their classwork. (8) Programs would air only before first period and during lunch, so no class time would be lost. (9) Student staff members would also need to keep at least a C average to stay on the team.

(10) Starting the station would not be expensive. (11) The school already owns microphones and laptops from a video course that ended last year, and free software can stream audio to the school website. (12) Radio was invented more than a hundred years ago. (13) So yeah, radio is awesome and we should totally do it.$q$, 'draft')
