   $q$Why does the writer include the phrase "a sac that normally holds waste" in sentence 13?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To give a statistic about how much water a tortoise drinks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-evidence"},{"text":"To explain what the bladder is so readers see why storing water there is unusual.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To show that the writer is unsure how tortoises store water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"To change the topic from water storage to digestion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To explain what the bladder is so readers see why storing water there is unusual.$q$, $q$The phrase defines "bladder" and shows that the organ usually has a different job, which makes the tortoise's water storage clear and surprising. The statistic about drinking appears in sentence 14, not in this phrase.$q$, 'draft', 'a0f980fb-185d-59aa-a8ef-4c606fd0c10c')
