-- Passage wg9-narrative-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('584bc29e-a68c-59ed-a30a-9bca81058f2a', 'wg9-narrative-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Point Fifteen$q$, $q$(1) The score was tied at fourteen, and the next point would decide the city ultimate championship. (2) I was the smallest player on the Harbor Street team, and for most of the season I had watched big games from the sideline. (3) Coach Ibarra pointed at me and said, "You're in for Dev." (4) My legs felt like they were filled with sand.

(5) We lined up on our goal line while the other team waited across the field. (6) The pull, a long throw that starts every point, floated high and landed near our end zone. (7) Our handler, Kalani, picked up the disc and looked for an open teammate. (8) For the first few passes, I mostly tried to stay out of the way. (9) Then I noticed that the defender guarding me kept watching the disc instead of me.

(10) I faked a step toward the sideline, then sprinted deep. (11) Kalani saw me and let the disc go, a long, curving throw that hung in the air for what felt like a full minute. (12) The wind pushed it left, and I adjusted, my cleats tearing at the grass. (13) I jumped, and the disc smacked into both of my hands just inside the end zone line. (14) My teammates rushed onto the field before my feet even touched the ground.

(15) Ultimate is played with seven players on each side of the field. (16) After the trophy photos, Coach Ibarra handed me the game disc, and I ran my thumb along the scuffs on its edge.$q$, 'draft')
