   $q$Why is it effective that Priyanka asks a question in sentence 10 rather than explaining the problem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shifts the point of view so the rest of the story is told by Priyanka.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-pov-shift"},{"text":"It shows that Priyanka does not understand how the app works.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It lets readers figure out the cause along with the narrator, making the discovery in sentence 12 more satisfying.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It slows the story down with a long description of daylight saving time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It lets readers figure out the cause along with the narrator, making the discovery in sentence 12 more satisfying.$q$, $q$The question hints at the answer, and the pause in sentence 11 lets readers make the connection just as the narrator does. The narrator, not Priyanka, continues telling the story.$q$, 'draft', '19660bd0-348e-5fca-a608-fdacf5119087')
