   $q$Which revision of sentence 9 best shows the narrator's thinking as the idea forms?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I looked through the window at the library's community room, empty except for stacked chairs, and started counting how many tables could fit along its walls.","is_correct":true},{"text":"I looked through the window at the library's community room, where the library holds meetings every month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"I looked through the window at the library's community room, which had gray carpet and tall windows.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-without-purpose"},{"text":"I looked through the window at the library's community room, and I felt very sad about the rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tells-not-shows"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I looked through the window at the library's community room, empty except for stacked chairs, and started counting how many tables could fit along its walls.$q$, $q$Counting tables shows the narrator already planning the move, which leads naturally to the question in sentence 10. Describing the carpet adds detail but does not reveal any thinking.$q$, 'draft', 'f664fd65-416f-5b05-b55d-097ce2c98b9d')
