-- Passage wg9-narrative-writing-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('3038fc80-0533-5a65-8633-c82595a9f2f4', 'wg9-narrative-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Control Six$q$, $q$(1) My first orienteering meet took place in Greystone State Forest on a cool October morning. (2) Each runner got a map, a compass, and a list of ten control points, which were orange and white flags hidden among the trees. (3) The goal was to find all ten in order as quickly as possible. (4) I had practiced reading maps in our school gym, but the gym did not have hills.

(5) The first four controls went smoothly. (6) I followed a stream to control five and found the flag beside a fallen oak. (7) At control six, everything changed. (8) The map showed a small pond, but in front of me was only a muddy field of reeds. (9) I turned in a slow circle. (10) Every tree looked like every other tree.

(11) I could have kept running and hoped to get lucky. (12) Instead, I sat on a stump, took a breath, and laid the map flat on my knee. (13) I lined the compass up with north and traced my route from control five. (14) That was when I realized the dry summer had shrunk the pond to mud. (15) I was in the right place after all. (16) The flag was hanging on a birch tree twenty steps away.

(17) Some people prefer hiking because it is more relaxing than racing. (18) I finished the course.$q$, 'draft')
