   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft states a clear claim that its evidence supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Arriaga shows that fog nets gave Las Brisas a reliable source of water and gave families back valuable time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Every dry village in the world should build fog nets on its hills before next year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Arriaga's article is about a village called Las Brisas and the fog that rolls in each morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Fog usually forms when warm, damp air passes over cooler ground or cooler water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Arriaga shows that fog nets gave Las Brisas a reliable source of water and gave families back valuable time.$q$, $q$The rest of the draft gives evidence about the water collected and the time saved, so the claim should name both. The choice about Las Brisas and the fog only names a topic and does not make a point the evidence can prove.$q$, 'draft', '2bfb5292-31b6-56a1-8b78-e11da4a5b6fe')
