   $q$Which revision of sentence 12 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Fog nets will completely end water problems in every village on every continent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Arriaga explains that tiny droplets cling to the mesh and run down into a gutter that feeds a tank.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"Arriaga's article shows that fog nets turned morning fog into thousands of liters of water and gave students hours of their day back.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Fog is also important because it keeps many coastal forests cool and damp.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Arriaga's article shows that fog nets turned morning fog into thousands of liters of water and gave students hours of their day back.$q$, $q$A strong conclusion restates the claim and ties together the two kinds of evidence, the water collected and the time saved. The choice about ending water problems everywhere goes far beyond one village's experience.$q$, 'draft', '2bfb5292-31b6-56a1-8b78-e11da4a5b6fe')
