  ('a11346bf-fd54-5e63-95a8-64ae6746b6cc', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A skeptical reader says the scores in sentence (9) might only mean the pilot class had stronger writers to begin with. Which added sentence would best address that objection?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The pilot students said the project was more enjoyable than any other assignment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-evidence"},{"text":"Most teachers agree that writing is one of the most important skills in school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-generalization"},{"text":"The department rubric was written by the history teachers several years ago.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The pilot class and the comparison classes had nearly identical writing scores at the start of the year.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The pilot class and the comparison classes had nearly identical writing scores at the start of the year.$q$, $q$If both groups started at the same level, the later difference is more likely linked to the project, which answers the objection directly. Student enjoyment may be true, but it says nothing about whether the groups began as equal writers.$q$, 'draft', '78f1f424-df33-5f4d-ae2b-9e30d8b747a8')
