  ('d705c08d-3c9a-5989-8278-f31a71ce3e55', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence (5) uses Bellmere as evidence. Which added detail would best show that Bellmere is a fair comparison to Tamsin Avenue?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bellmere's council voted unanimously for the lanes after a long public meeting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-off-point"},{"text":"Like Tamsin Avenue, Bellmere's street carried similar daily traffic and passed two schools.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many cities across the country have been building more bike lanes in recent years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Bellmere's lanes were painted bright green so that drivers would notice them easily.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"describes-not-compares"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Like Tamsin Avenue, Bellmere's street carried similar daily traffic and passed two schools.$q$, $q$A comparison is only convincing if the two streets are alike, and the correct detail shows similar traffic and nearby schools. The vote and the paint color describe Bellmere's lanes but never show that the streets are comparable.$q$, 'draft', '101d4c66-b8d7-5ec3-9cc9-968e616112bd')
