  ('db4d1504-57d5-515b-af55-393e0c4e5ea4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (12) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Commuters who dislike music should simply find some other way to get to work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"The council should also paint the waiting hall a brighter color sometime next year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"With sensible hours and placement, a piano would make the station more welcoming and give musicians an audience.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In the end, music is one of the greatest inventions in all of human history.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With sensible hours and placement, a piano would make the station more welcoming and give musicians an audience.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion sums up the benefits and the solutions to the noise concern from sentence (9). The statement about music in history is too general and drops the claim about Eastbrook Station.$q$, 'draft', 'b5feffd2-fb85-56b2-be1b-fa72651b83d9')
