   $q$Which statement best describes how the writer handles the evidence in sentence (5)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The writer reports a result but avoids claiming the piano definitely caused it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The writer admits that the piano made the waiting area less clean.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-evidence"},{"text":"The writer introduces an opposing claim and then answers it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-function"},{"text":"The writer proves that the piano was the only reason litter decreased.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The writer reports a result but avoids claiming the piano definitely caused it.$q$, $q$The word "possibly" shows the writer is careful not to overstate what the litter data proves, which keeps the reasoning honest. The sentence does not claim proof, so the choice "The writer proves that the piano was the only reason litter decreased" misreads it.$q$, 'draft', 'b5feffd2-fb85-56b2-be1b-fa72651b83d9')
