   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence (9), would best strengthen the response to the noise concern in sentence (7)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Pianos come in many sizes, from small uprights to large concert grands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Music has been shown to improve people's moods in many situations.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"In Wren Harbor's survey, only 4 percent said the piano made calls or announcements harder to hear.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some commuters already listen to music through earbuds while they wait.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-off-point"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In Wren Harbor's survey, only 4 percent said the piano made calls or announcements harder to hear.$q$, $q$The correct choice gives specific evidence that noise was rarely a problem in a similar setting, which directly answers sentence (7). The general claim about mood does not address whether the piano interferes with calls or rest.$q$, 'draft', 'b5feffd2-fb85-56b2-be1b-fa72651b83d9')
