   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (13) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The commission should also build a larger parking lot at the forest entrance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"In the end, every tree in every forest deserves to be protected forever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Treating the streamside hemlocks now would keep the trout streams cool until the beetle is ready, which neither waiting nor replanting can do.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Residents who want to let nature take its course simply do not care about trout.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Treating the streamside hemlocks now would keep the trout streams cool until the beetle is ready, which neither waiting nor replanting can do.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and reflects the writer's answers to both opposing views. The statement about every tree overreaches and loses the specific focus on streamside hemlocks.$q$, 'draft', 'df3f57e2-4c90-55ba-8db2-54649a4d7cd1')
