   $q$Which sentence about a pottery class uses a semicolon correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After the clay bowls dried overnight; the class glazed them in bright colors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-after-dependent-clause"},{"text":"The clay bowls dried overnight; and the class glazed them in bright colors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-with-conjunction"},{"text":"The clay bowls dried overnight; the next morning, the class glazed them in bright colors.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The class glazed the bowls in; bright blue, green, and orange.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-misplaced"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The clay bowls dried overnight; the next morning, the class glazed them in bright colors.$q$, $q$Both "The clay bowls dried overnight" and "the next morning, the class glazed them in bright colors" are independent clauses, so the semicolon is correct. In "After the clay bowls dried overnight; the class glazed them," the opening "After the clay bowls dried overnight" is a dependent clause and needs a comma, not a semicolon.$q$, 'draft', null)
