   $q$Read the sentence: "The art club's supply order included items such as: charcoal pencils, watercolor paper, and fine brushes." Which revision corrects the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The art club's supply order included items such as charcoal pencils, watercolor paper, and fine brushes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The art club's supply order included items such as; charcoal pencils, watercolor paper, and fine brushes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-colon"},{"text":"The art club's supply order included: items such as charcoal pencils, watercolor paper, and fine brushes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"},{"text":"The art club's supply order included items such as, charcoal pencils, watercolor paper, and fine brushes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-such-as"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The art club's supply order included items such as charcoal pencils, watercolor paper, and fine brushes.$q$, $q$"Such as" already introduces the examples, and the words before it are not a complete clause, so no punctuation belongs after it. Replacing the colon with a semicolon or a comma still breaks the sentence at the wrong point.$q$, 'draft', null)
