   $q$Read the sentence: "The weather balloon rose to nearly 30 kilometers the thin air caused it to swell until it burst." Where is a semicolon needed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After \"swell\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-dependent-clause"},{"text":"After \"kilometers\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"After \"air\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-splits-subject-verb"},{"text":"After \"balloon\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-splits-subject-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After "kilometers"$q$, $q$The first independent clause ends with "kilometers," and the second begins with "the thin air caused," so the semicolon goes after "kilometers." A semicolon after "swell" would leave "until it burst," a dependent clause, on its own.$q$, 'draft', null)
