   $q$Read the sentences: "The library extended its weekend hours. Attendance at the homework help sessions doubled." Which choice combines them correctly using a transitional phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The library extended its weekend hours, as a result, attendance at the homework help sessions doubled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-with-adverb"},{"text":"The library extended its weekend hours; as a result attendance, at the homework help sessions doubled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misplaced"},{"text":"The library extended its weekend hours; as a result, attendance at the homework help sessions doubled.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The library extended its weekend hours as a result; attendance at the homework help sessions doubled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-after-adverb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The library extended its weekend hours; as a result, attendance at the homework help sessions doubled.$q$, $q$"As a result" works like a conjunctive adverb, so it follows the semicolon and is set off by a comma. Putting the semicolon after "as a result" attaches the transition to the wrong clause, making the cause and effect unclear.$q$, 'draft', null)
