  ('8765f91c-bb23-5136-a4db-518fa2cab247', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Fog makes the crossing unsafe, so the ferry will leave on schedule only ___ the fog lifts by noon." Which choice best completes the adverbial clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"although","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shows-contrast-not-condition"},{"text":"whereas","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shows-contrast-not-condition"},{"text":"if","is_correct":true},{"text":"unless","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-condition"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$if$q$, $q$The ferry can leave on time only on the condition that the fog lifts, so "if" creates the needed conditional clause. "Unless" reverses the logic, suggesting the ferry leaves on time only when the fog does not lift.$q$, 'draft', null)
