  ('9f9717e0-cd60-588f-9ae2-8d34bd58aaa6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Kenji worked weekends at the bakery to buy a secondhand telescope." How does the phrase "to buy a secondhand telescope" function?$q$, $q$[{"text":"as a noun phrase serving as the subject","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-adverbial"},{"text":"as an absolute phrase describing the whole scene","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-absolute-infinitive"},{"text":"as an adjectival phrase describing \"bakery\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-adjectival-adverbial"},{"text":"as an adverbial phrase telling why Kenji worked","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$as an adverbial phrase telling why Kenji worked$q$, $q$The infinitive phrase explains the purpose of the verb "worked," answering "Why?" so it functions adverbially. It does not describe the bakery, so it is not adjectival.$q$, 'draft', null)
