  ('bf20e38e-ccbd-5f7a-a69d-cf62fb459776', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The report concluded that the river was cleaner than it had been a decade earlier, that fish populations had grown, and ___." Which choice completes the sentence with parallel structure?$q$, $q$[{"text":"more families using the trails along its banks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-missing-verb"},{"text":"that more families were using the trails along its banks","is_correct":true},{"text":"families using the trails, which had increased","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"noun-phrase-breaks-parallel"},{"text":"an increase in families using the trails along its banks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"noun-phrase-breaks-parallel"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$that more families were using the trails along its banks$q$, $q$The report's conclusions are a series of noun clauses beginning with "that," so the third item should be a "that" clause too. "More families using the trails" has no complete verb and does not match the two clauses before it.$q$, 'draft', null)
