  ('9bd89384-7104-59a8-b3be-fb1cddb45950', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The sculpture stood beside the fountain that the students carved from reclaimed wood." The students carved the sculpture. Which revision places the relative clause so that it clearly describes the sculpture?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sculpture stood that the students carved from reclaimed wood beside the fountain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"scrambled-word-order"},{"text":"The sculpture stood beside the fountain, that the students carved from reclaimed wood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-relative-clause"},{"text":"The sculpture that the students carved from reclaimed wood stood beside the fountain.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Beside the fountain that the students carved from reclaimed wood stood the sculpture.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-relative-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sculpture that the students carved from reclaimed wood stood beside the fountain.$q$, $q$A relative clause describes the noun right before it, so the clause must follow "sculpture." In the other choices the clause still follows "fountain" or interrupts the verb phrase, which makes it seem the fountain was carved.$q$, 'draft', null)
