  ('0be0caf4-b599-531e-80ee-452e9ded2f0f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The best time to see the comet is just before dawn." How does the phrase "to see the comet" function?$q$, $q$[{"text":"as an adjectival phrase modifying \"time\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"as an absolute phrase modifying the whole sentence","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-absolute-infinitive"},{"text":"as an adverbial phrase modifying \"is\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-adjectival-adverbial"},{"text":"as a noun phrase serving as the subject","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-noun-adjectival"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$as an adjectival phrase modifying "time"$q$, $q$The infinitive phrase tells which time is meant, so it describes the noun "time" and works as an adjective. The subject is "The best time," not the infinitive phrase, so it is not a noun phrase here.$q$, 'draft', null)
