  ('4f8453c0-71c6-5a87-8ae8-2ff1dc8c365a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence uses parallel structure correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The internship taught Lucia how to build a website, testing it, and to explain its features to clients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms-in-series"},{"text":"The internship taught Lucia how to build a website, how to test it, and how to explain its features to clients.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The internship taught Lucia to build a website, test it, and how to explain its features to clients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms-in-series"},{"text":"The internship taught Lucia building a website, to test it, and explaining its features to clients.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-forms-in-series"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The internship taught Lucia how to build a website, how to test it, and how to explain its features to clients.$q$, $q$Each item in the correct sentence follows the same "how to" plus verb pattern. The choice "The internship taught Lucia to build a website, test it, and how to explain its features to clients" starts with plain infinitives but switches to "how to" for the last item, so the series is not parallel.$q$, 'draft', null)
